@h3 text 16:9
style: live-action, cinematic, warm evening light, one continuous take
context: 22
MUSIC: a slow acoustic guitar melody plays under everything

SCENE the bridge
SHOT 5s: tracking, slow
A young woman with short black hair in a mustard-yellow raincoat and a tall man with a grey beard in a dark green wool coat walk side by side across a wooden footbridge over a river at dusk, talking and gesturing.
WOMAN (laughing): You said the boat would wait for us.
SFX: footsteps on wooden planks; water rushing below
END ON: the woman and the man stop at the end of the bridge

SCENE the lanterns
SHOT 5s: pan right, slow
The young woman with short black hair in a mustard-yellow raincoat points up at a row of paper lanterns lighting up along the riverbank, while the tall man with a grey beard in a dark green wool coat turns to look.
MAN (softly): They light them every night at this hour.
SFX: a gentle breeze; distant voices on the water
END ON: the woman and the man look up at the lanterns

SCENE the stairs
SHOT 5s: tracking, slow
The young woman with short black hair in a mustard-yellow raincoat runs down a flight of stone steps toward the water, and the tall man with a grey beard in a dark green wool coat follows her, holding the railing.
WOMAN (calling back): Come on, we can still catch it!
SFX: quick footsteps on stone; the man's heavy breathing
END ON: the woman reaches the bottom step by the water

SCENE the boat
SHOT 5s: pull out, slow
A small wooden boat with a lantern on its bow drifts away from the jetty while the young woman with short black hair in a mustard-yellow raincoat and the tall man with a grey beard in a dark green wool coat wave at it from the shore, laughing.
MAN (laughing): Next time we'll be early.
SFX: water lapping against the jetty; a bell rings on the boat
END ON: the boat glides away into the dusk
